    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_quadratic_gap_four_paired_all_excess_residual_fiber_factorization",
    "title": "A=1 quadratic paired all-excess residual-fiber factorization",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exact fiber factorization and first jet at every off-line slope",
    "statement": "For every off-line supported slope in either paired profile, the split-biform fiber factors as the actual-inside locator, a nonzero residual polynomial of degree at most the union excess, and the complete padded-heavy factor. Its X-degree drop is exactly the union excess minus the residual-polynomial degree. The residual polynomial is coprime to the outside-support locator, so the vertical common roots are exactly actual-inside support plus padding. Every actual-support root is a transverse intersection of the two global curves.",
